  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "9ee5990f-96b5-4a62-be40-01951f5379c0",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "Students who have listed on their transcript completion of an ADT or IGETC, CSUGE, or CALGETC certification will waive all General Education except for the following: World Languages (L), Writing in the Discipline (WD), Information and Media Literacy Advanced (IMLA), and Community Service Activity (CSAC). Writing requirements are determined by writing pathways chosen by the student. **First Year Seminar (FYS)** is waived for transfer students with 12 or more semester units earned upon transfer. First year students with any number of units are still required to take a FYS course. **C, H, S, N, L** may not double count with each other. Each course fulfilling this section must be distinct from each other course in this section. **APW, CPI, ESS, TG** may double count in this section OR in the section above. A course meeting a requirement in this section may only fulfill one other requirement in this section or the above section. **QRF, QRE** may double count with any requirement. When transferring two QRF courses, both QRF and QRE will be fulfilled upon transfer.",
      "contentHtml": "<p>Students who have listed on their transcript completion of an ADT or IGETC, CSUGE, or CALGETC certification will waive all General Education except for the following: World Languages (L), Writing in the Discipline (WD), Information and Media Literacy Advanced (IMLA), and Community Service Activity (CSAC).</p><p><br></p><p>Writing requirements are determined by writing pathways chosen by the student. </p><p><br></p><p>**First Year Seminar (FYS)** is waived for transfer students with 12 or more semester units earned upon transfer. First year students with any number of units are still required to take a FYS course.</p><p><br></p><p>**C, H, S, N, L** may not double count with each other. Each course fulfilling this section must be distinct from each other course in this section.</p><p>**APW, CPI, ESS, TG** may double count in this section OR in the section above. A course meeting a requirement in this section may only fulfill one other requirement in this section or the above section.</p><p><br></p><p>**QRF, QRE** may double count with any requirement. When transferring two QRF courses, both QRF and QRE will be fulfilled upon transfer.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>"
    }
  ],
